data_vte2
# Phase identity: ambient distorted 1T'' VTe2, C2/m, conventional source cell.
# Provenance: Bronsema, Bus & Wiegers, J. Solid State Chem. 53, 415--421
# (1984), COD 1535594 (CC0). The source sample is V1.04Te2; because its minor
# interstitial V site is not part of the supplied coordinate packet and partial
# occupancies are rejected by cxr-mc, this model explicitly idealizes the fully
# occupied primary sites to stoichiometric VTe2. It is not the high-T trigonal phase.
# The P1 basis expands the reported 2a, 4i, and 4j sites in the source setting.
# Limiting checks: V=abc sin(beta), 6V+12Te, and finite basal (001) coupling.
# Validation: vte2-c2m-structure
